questions.question_text:
Find the points of intersection of the parabola $y=x^{2}$ and the line $y=x+6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4, xmax=4, ymin=-2, ymax=11, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.3:3.3] {x*x};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-4:4] {x+6};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:-2.9,10.3) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:3.0,10.4) {$y=x+6$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the points of intersection of the parabola $y=x^{2}-4x$ and the line $y=5$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-2, xmax=6, ymin=-5, ymax=7.5, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.32:5.32] {x*x-4*x};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-1.6:5.8] {5};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:-1.3,6.6) {$y=x^{2}-4x$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:4.7,5.5) {$y=5$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the point(s) of intersection of the parabola $y=x^{2}$ and the line $y=4x-4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.5, xmax=5, ymin=-1, ymax=10, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-1:3.16] {x*x};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=0.75:3.5] {4*x-4};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:-1.05,9) {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:3.6,9.4) {$y=4x-4$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the points of intersection of the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}=25$ and the line $x+y=7$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.4]
\draw[->] (-6.5,0)--(6.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-6.5)--(0,6.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \n in {5,-5} {\draw (\n,-0.15)--(\n,0.15); \draw (-0.15,\n)--(0.15,\n);}
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) circle (5);
\draw[thick,red,<->] (1.5,5.5)--(6.3,0.7);
\node[blue] at (-3.2,5.6) {$x^{2}+y^{2}=25$};
\node[red] at (5.8,4.3) {$x+y=7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the points of intersection of the hyperbola $y=\dfrac{8}{x}$ and the line $y=2x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-5, xmax=5, ymin=-8, ymax=8, samples=100, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=1:4.5] {8/x};
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-4.5:-1] {8/x};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-3.8:3.8] {2*x};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:3.9,3.1) {$y=\frac{8}{x}$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:2.4,7.2) {$y=2x$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The parabola $y=x^{2}-3$ and the line $y=2x$ are shown. Use the graph to read off the two points of intersection.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3.5, xmax=4.5, ymin=-4.5, ymax=7.5, grid=both, minor tick num=0, xtick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4}, ytick={-4,-2,2,4,6}, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, tick label style={font=\scriptsize}]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.06:3.06] {x*x-3};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-1.8:3.5] {2*x};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:-2.6,4.6) {$y=x^{2}-3$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:3.4,6.4) {$y=2x$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A delivery drone follows the path $y=x^{2}-4x+6$, and a straight guide wire runs along $y=x+2$ (with $x$ and $y$ in metres). Find the coordinates of the points where the path crosses the wire.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1, xmax=6, ymin=0, ymax=10, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-0.83:4.83] {x*x-4*x+6};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-1:6] {x+2};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:0.4,9.2) {$y=x^{2}-4x+6$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:5.3,8.6) {$y=x+2$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does the line $y=x-4$ meet the parabola $y=x^{2}+1$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3, xmax=3, ymin=-4, ymax=6, samples=80, clip=false, axis line style={->}, xtick=\empty, ytick=\empty]
\addplot[smooth,thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.2:2.2] {x*x+1};
\addplot[thick,red,<->,domain=-1:3] {x-4};
\node[blue] at (axis cs:-1.9,5.6) {$y=x^{2}+1$};
\node[red] at (axis cs:2.6,-0.4) {$y=x-4$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
